  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Amentum Services has $3B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Amentum Services received 1,160 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $2.6M. Obligations are down 15.5% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations rose from $1.4B in FY21 to $3.8B in FY24, then fell to $3.5B in FY25 and to $3B in FY26. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1.9B so far in FY2026. The Department of Homeland Security is the second-largest buyer with $787M in obligations. Other notable buyers include the General Services Administration at $129M and the Department of the Treasury at $87.3M. Amentum Services’ largest markets by NAICS are Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $1B, Security Guards and Patrol Services at $508M, and Engineering Services at $425M. Facilities Support Services, Computer Facilities Management Services, and General Warehousing and Storage also appear among the top markets, with obligations of $253M, $155M, and $153M respectively.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Amentum Services' federal business changed year over year?",
        "body": "Amentum Services obligated $3B in FY2026 to date, down 15.5% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations climbed from $1.4B in FY21 to $3.8B in FY24, then moved to $3.5B in FY25 and $3B in FY26. The number of awards this fiscal year to date is 1,160 and the average award size is $2.6M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Amentum Services' largest federal customers and markets?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1.9B, followed by the Department of Homeland Security at $787M, the General Services Administration at $129M, and the Department of the Treasury at $87.3M. The largest markets are Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $1B, Security Guards and Patrol Services at $508M, and Engineering Services at $425M, with Facilities Support Services at $253M and Computer Facilities Management Services at $155M rounding out the top areas."
      }
    ]
